  "expected_claims": [
    "The Overheat Saws displayed scalar and melee_project FIREBURN scalar have the same t.getDamage origin; application occurs only for living targets of successful melee hits.",
    "A scalar FIREBURN input defaults to dur=3 and initial=50, so half is projected immediately and the other half becomes a three-turn BURNING contribution; the incoming scalar is the complete event amount before downstream mitigation.",
    "BURNING reapplication supports the English stacking statement by pooling old remaining and new incoming remaining damage and recomputing duration/power; it does not preserve an isolated new-effect tick schedule.",
    "The two elemental-trap descriptions are generic templates shared across acid, fire, ice, lightning and poison variants; their formatter arguments preserve color, scalar amount, localized damage-type name and, for the blast, runtime radius.",
    "For fire trap instances the dynamic localized damage-type name is 火焰燃烧; the fire blast binds radius=2, and the generic template fallback is also 2."
  ],
  "exclusions": [
    "No reference outside fireburn-ref-008, fireburn-ref-020 and fireburn-ref-021.",
